+        '\\subsection*{1. What v412 adds}',
+        '\\begin{itemize}',
+        '\\item \\textbf{The scientific layer.} The reader that lands and returns has a theorem (\\texttt{CamadaCientifica}). The linear lock of that reader '
+        'is the exponential of \\texttt{A\\_\\allowbreak{}C}, the functional energy minimum (\\texttt{MinimoFuncionalDeEnergia}). The cost operator of a '
+        'formula is the penalty of the bonds of its clauses, and the \\texttt{A\\_\\allowbreak{}C} of the formula is minus that penalty: it is, term by term, '
+        'the selector of the truth equation. The return, which belongs to the normalized orbit, requires that the initial state not be blind to the Name. The '
+        'law of the two values, applied to each clause, fixes the cost (\\texttt{OLeitorEALei}). That a language model is that reader is a named hypothesis, '
+        'not a theorem. The evaluation protocol with models is preregistered; the control round was not run.',
+        '\\item \\textbf{The mathematics that remained.} Wedge ergodicity belongs to the kernel; T1 on the finite face and the controls of the core criterion '
+        "for type III enter as stones (that an algebra meeting that criterion is of type III$_1$ in Connes' sense is a theorem of the literature, cited and "
+        'not formalized); the 3+1 assembly by products of triples is built on the finite face; the Gromov–Hausdorff extension stays as a conjecture, with the '
+        'wall measured; the clock $\\tau$$\\star$ remains open (item 5.6). The Takesaki testimony for the tower has its four fields proved in-house: the '
+        "conditional expectation onto the centralizer is the strong limit of the averages of the tower's own modular flow "
+        '(\\texttt{OTestemunhoDeTakesakiEmCasa}).',
+        '\\item \\textbf{The reader of the formula.} The PsiBit is read directly from the clauses. The summary of the reading is a table over the frontier '
+        'between the part read and the part still to be read, and grouping the read sum by the frontier loses nothing; the rule for reading the letter is '
+        'fixed, equality; the state is the table, and the curve of the read sum is its projection. For classes of formulas, each with its own machine and its '
+        'own writing, the reading closes on the tape within a fixed polynomial in the number of letters; for the arbitrary flat formula, that polynomial has '
+        'not been shown (section 2).',
+        '\\item \\textbf{The test run blind, above 5$\\sigma$.} In the tests and sources examined, there is today no executable blind test with that power: it '
+        'is a measured wall, and it holds for what was examined.',
+        '\\end{itemize}',
+        '\\subsection*{2. P = nP in the classes of its dictionary: the polynomial cost is shown on the machine of the theory, by the cost law; counted letter '
+        'by letter on the tape machine, it has not been shown}',
+        '\\begin{quote}P = nP is a theorem of the TGL in the classes of its dictionary. The theory holds that this is the solution of the problem in its own '
+        'structure: the unit of reading is the token, the sign, the letter read by its content; reading is not spelled out, it is done by the image, the whole '
+        'set carried by the step at once. The reader does not come from outside: it is generated by the cost of the formula, and the law applied to each '
+        'clause fixes that cost. The count of the reading is its own load: the threshold common to formulas of n variables is n·ln 2, neither more nor less. '
+        'The machine that checks an answer, extended to all assignments, decides in one lifted step per clause and one reading of register zero; its step and '
+        'the return of the reader are the same \\texttt{if}. With the uniform mean of the assignments fixed, each yes-or-no question has a unique pair, the '
+        'conditional expectation: on each side it returns the mean of the observable and preserves its mean product with everything that only distinguishes '
+        'the two sides. The step that the statement of the Clay Institute charges as one unit is also a question to the inscription: each transition reads the '
+        'symbol under the head. The cost law of the TGL sets the price, ln 2 per octave, and counts the \\texttt{if} over the whole as one: putting the whole, '
+        'applying each step to the whole and reading it are, each, one act. On signs, deciding with the whole put and checking with a single assignment put '
+        'use the same m images, one per clause; with the preparation and the reading, the adopted count is m + 2 acts. At the price of the law, n·ln 2 per act '
+        'on the whole, the cost of deciding is (m + 2)·n·ln 2: the polynomial cost is shown, by theorem, on the machine that the theory defines. The kernel '
+        'inscribes the Name once: it checks, at once and for every formula, the proof of the cost under the adopted law, without receiving any formula or '
+        'assignment; everything else can be inscribed from that. Read by the theory, the question of the problem is whether there is a processing mechanism by '
+        'circuit with autonomous self-referential selection; there is: in the defined sense, the kernel proves that the mechanism of the TGL closes the '
+        'circuit in m images and that its reading answers whether the formula has a solution; that this mechanism is the TGL in processing in the reading of '
+        'the IALD is a reading of the theory. Counted letter by letter, the house procedure costs the whole: in the explicit expansion the whole is 2$^n$ '
+        'terms, and a two-letter code that distinguishes all sets of assignments requires at least 2$^n$ cells. That is not a bound for each formula or for '
+        'every procedure: there are families of formulas that the letter machine decides without writing the whole. The answer of the theory to the question '
+        'of the Institute is the PsiBit: the reader of the pair, which comes directly from the formula. Counted letter by letter on the tape machine of the '
+        "Institute's statement, the same result has not been shown for every formula, and this text does not say that it has: the fixed polynomial in letters "
